    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="0632" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg534"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Geldart to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-12-22"><hi rendition="#italic">December 22,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I read in the files of yesterday’s papers,
                    re stoppage of merchandise shipped from this port to Delagoa Bay, that you had
                    not as yet received any official complaint.</p>
                <p>I had the honor of addressing you on this subject the 15th instant, and beg to
                    inclose for your further guidance the original of a communication recently
                    received from the local agents of the steamship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Beatrice</hi>, sailing under the British flag, which is
                    self-explanatory.</p>
                <p>These particular goods consisted of American beer and lard, and I am extremely
                    surprised at the action of the English authorities and would be glad to hear
                    that you are doing something to extricate us from a serious difficulty.</p>
                <pb facs="0633" n="535" xml:id="pg535"/>
                <p>This shipment was made to a Portuguese subject at Lourenco Marquez, and was
                    merely a repeat order of similar merchandise forwarded at different times this
                    year.</p>
                <p>I also learn from the papers that a lot of provisions per steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Mashona</hi> had been seized by the English authorities
                    at Cape Town, and which were intended for Delagoa Bay; this also I am interested
                    in, and unless prompt action be taken in the matter, American citizens acting in
                    good faith are liable to make serious losses.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. W. Geldart.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d647-a1.xml" xpointer="d647-a1"/>
